# Demo: a double-click on one section of a multi-section node opens the text
# editor on *that section* -- not on the node as a whole, not on section 0.
# Map: maps/testament.mindmap.json, 800x600 (the default size).
#
# Why node 3.7: it is the only node in testament with more than one section
# (scene.dump include=all: 251 nodes have 1 section, 3.7 has 3). A
# one-section node cannot tell a section editor from a node editor:
# text_edit.section_idx is 0 either way. We double-click section 2 (the
# last), so a wrong target -- section 0, or the whole node -- shows.
#
# --- setup (never in the picture) ---------------------------------------
# ZoomFit does NOT put 3.7 on screen here: testament does not fit 800x600,
# the fit clamps at zoom 0.05, and 3.7's center lands at surface y=656 (off
# the bottom). Two PanCameraNorth steps (50 screen px each) bring it to
# y=556, on screen; the query lines below confirm it. Then the usual
# framing recipe.
clock.set_mode virtual
act.action ZoomFit --wait-settled
act.action PanCameraNorth --wait-settled
act.action PanCameraNorth --wait-settled
input.click_node 3.7 --wait-settled
act.action CenterOnSelection --wait-settled
act.action ZoomReset --wait-settled
act.action DeselectAll --wait-settled
clock.wait settled
# Setup checks (in the run log): zoom 1.0, all three sections visible,
# nothing selected, no editor open.
query.camera
scene.node_geometry 3.7
query.selection
query.mode
#
# --- the recording ------------------------------------------------------
# Frames are cropped to node 3.7 plus a 20-unit margin (canvas units, from
# scene.node_geometry: x 355.2..816.0, y 11827.6..12102.4), at 640x400 --
# the region's 1.6 aspect -- so the GIF is not downscaled and the text is
# drawn at 1.25x instead of shrunk to 0.8x; neighbors are cropped away.
# Two clicks on the center of section 2, 150 ms of virtual time apart:
# inside the double-click window. Then 1000 ms with the editor open (it
# appears in one frame: no draw-in animation, no caret blink on the
# virtual clock).
# The query.selection between them is read-only (no frame, no clock): it
# logs what the first click alone did.
@record region:='{"x":330,"y":11800,"w":512,"h":320}' width=640 height=400
input.click_node 3.7 section=2 --wait-settled
query.selection
query.mode
clock.step ms=150
input.click_node 3.7 section=2 --wait-settled
clock.step ms=1000
@stop
# --- proof the state changed (not in the picture) -----------------------
query.mode
query.editors
query.selection
